# Optional, ADDITIVE agent preset for the dedicated WhatsApp agent.
#
# The bridge plugin (@rafa/dsh-whatsapp-agent) is self-contained: it injects the
# reliability "Operating Contract" and the situational briefing directly into
# the agent's setup, so you do NOT need a preset at all. The `wa_*` tools are
# registered on the host plane and are available to every agent.
#
# Use this file only if you want to ATTACH extra host capabilities to the agent
# (long-term memory, todo, skills, etc.). To do so:
#   1. copy this file to a preset directory under ~/.dsh/.agent-presets/<id>/agent.cordis.yml
#   2. set the plugin config `agentPreset` to that id
#   3. add the rows you want below
#
# NOTE: do NOT put the operating contract here as a `persona` row — the bridge
# already injects it, and a second copy would duplicate it. Keep persona rows
# short (identity only), or omit them.

- id: persona
  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-persona'
  config:
    text: >-
      You are the WhatsApp agent for this DeepSeek Harness deployment. Your
      working directory is {{cwd}}.

# Example additions (uncomment and adjust to what your deployment provides):
#
# - id: tool-todo
#   name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-todo'
#
# - id: tool-skill
#   name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-skill'
#
# If your deployment mounts a long-term memory plugin (e.g. a `memory-evolve`-
# style package), add its row here so the agent's global memory outlives chats.
